remstart
    THE DEMO
    when the main menu has been left alone for a while, the game plays itself, the way that an arcade
    machine does: the bubbles take the menu away, a game is dealt, and "DEMO MODE" blinks over it while
    a player that is not there makes the moves. anything at all that is pressed stops it, and the bubbles
    bring the menu back.

    a demo is a show of a few SCENES, one after another, with a wave of bubbles between them, and each one
    shows off something that the game does not say out loud: the night that falls when the tide goes in and
    out, the schools that swim off, a late round with stingrays and jellyfish, and last of all, the diver
    that a bottle brings down. so it is a hint, too. after the diver, the bubbles bring the menu back.

    the moves are not a recording. a recording only plays back the same game while the rules and the deal
    of its seed stay the same, and they change whenever the game is balanced. so the scene sets the game
    up, and the demo player picks its own moves, every time: the swap that pops the most, near where the
    cursor is, with a little luck in it so that no two demos are alike. it walks the cursor there a step at
    a time, and then swaps, like a person would.

    nothing that happens in a demo is kept. the preferences are in a sandbox for as long as it lasts (see
    `begin pref sandbox`), so the saved game, the codec and everything else in prefs.json are left alone,
    and the few things that are kept in memory too are not touched while DEMO_MODE is 1: codecSeeCard,
    modSet, morseBottle, save_game, forget_saved_game, the steam timeline. a demo round never gets the
    upgrade screen (the bar empties out and the next round starts, the way that it does in a zen game),
    and a demo never ends a game: the end of a game, or an ending, stops the demo instead.

    fish_routines_demo has the rest. what the rest of the game does for it:
    - the main loop does `gosub frame_demo` on every frame, before anything else looks at the menu.
    - update_frame calls demoTick() on every frame, so that the banner blinks, and a press is heard,
      even while fish are popping.
    for trying it out: FISH_DEMO_IDLE_MS sets how long the menu has to be left alone, FISH_DEMO_LENGTH_MS
    how long a scene lasts (the last one too), and FISH_DEMO_SCENE plays only that scene (1 to
    DEMO_SCENE_COUNT), and then stops.
remend

global DEMO_MODE = 0 `1 while the game is playing itself
global DEMO_IDLE_MS = 30000 `how long the main menu has to be left alone before a demo starts
` the options page can turn the demo off. then the main menu can be left alone for as long as anybody likes.
#constant PREF_DEMO 22
global OPTION_DEMO = 1 `1 while a demo is wanted
global DEMO_LENGTH_MS = 40000 `how long a scene plays for. it moves on at the first quiet moment after this.
global DEMO_LENGTH_LAST_MS = 55000 `and the last one, the diver, which needs the time to dive, take its pictures, and go back up
global DEMO_IDLE_FROM = 0 `when the menu was last touched, on the clock of the game
global DEMO_MENU_FRAME = -10 `the last frame that the main menu was looked at. a page of its own in between does not count as being left alone.
global DEMO_STARTED_MS = 0
global DEMO_STOP_WANTED = 0 `1 once something has been pressed

` THE SCENES are played one after another, in this order, with a wave of bubbles between them, and the
` diver is always the last: its reveal is the end of the show. after it, the bubbles bring the menu back.
global DEMO_SCENE_COUNT = 5
global DEMO_SCENE_BASICS = 1 `the first round: swaps, and pops
global DEMO_SCENE_NIGHT = 2 `the tide turns, night falls, the groups wait for the morning, and the morning pops them
global DEMO_SCENE_SCHOOL = 3 `every fish faces the same way, so the groups swim off as schools
global DEMO_SCENE_LATE = 4 `a late round, with cards, stingrays, jellyfish and a big multiplier
global DEMO_SCENE_DIVER = 5 `a bottle is carried up to the top row, and the diver comes down to take pictures. always the last.
global DEMO_SCENE = 0 `the scene that is playing
global DEMO_SCENE_ONLY = 0 `a scene to play on its own, and then stop, from FISH_DEMO_SCENE. 0 plays them all.
global DEMO_NIGHT_AFTER = 2 `in the night scene, night falls after this many swaps

` THE PLAYER. it thinks, walks the cursor to the swap, and swaps, and then waits for the board to settle.
global DEMO_STATE = 0 `0 thinking, 1 walking, 2 waiting for the swap to play out
global DEMO_THINK_UNTIL = 0 `when it has thought for long enough
global DEMO_THINK_MS = 350 `how long it thinks, at the least
global DEMO_THINK_MORE_MS = 400 `and up to this much more
global DEMO_STEP_MS = 120 `how long a step of the cursor takes
global DEMO_STEP_AT = 0 `when the next step can be taken
global DEMO_TARGET = 0 `the cell that the cursor walks to
global DEMO_DIR_X = 1 `and the way that it swaps from there
global DEMO_DIR_Y = 0
global DEMO_SCRIPTED = 0 `1 when the scene has picked the next swap itself, so the player does not pick one
global DEMO_SWAPS = 0 `how many swaps it has made in this demo
global DEMO_MOVES_BEFORE = 0 `the count of moves and the score just before the swap, to tell whether it did anything
global DEMO_SCORE_BEFORE = 0
global DEMO_NIGHT_BEFORE = 0 `the moves that the night had left, or 0 in the day
global DEMO_LAST_CELL = -1 `the swap it made last, which it does not make again straight away: that would undo it
global DEMO_LAST_DOWN = 0
global DEMO_BAN_COUNT = 0 `swaps that did nothing. they are not tried again until the score moves.
global dim DEMO_BAN_CELL(64)
global dim DEMO_BAN_DOWN(64)
global dim DEMO_MARK(400) `for counting the fish of a group. a cell is counted when its mark is DEMO_STAMP.
global dim DEMO_STACK(400)
global DEMO_STAMP = 0
global DEMO_TOUCHES_DIVER = 0 `1 when the group that was counted last is next to the diver
global DEMO_SWAP_DIVER = 0 `1 when the swap that was weighed last pops a group next to the diver, which can be photographed
global DEMO_DIVER_X = -10 `where the diver is, while the swaps are weighed. far off the board when there is none.
global DEMO_DIVER_Y = -10

` THE BANNER
global DEMO_TEXT_ID = 0
global DEMO_BLINK_ON_MS = 650 `it shows for this long
global DEMO_BLINK_OFF_MS = 400 `and is gone for this long
global DEMO_BANNER_Y = 0 `setup_demo works it out
global ORDER_DEMO = 150 `on top of the board, the info screen and the overlay bubbles, and under the menu, whose bubbles wipe it away
